## Publishing an App Release (full checklist)

This is the end-to-end process to ship an update that every user's copy of Meridian will automatically detect and offer to install.

### Prerequisites

- Xcode Developer ID Application certificate in your keychain (for signing)
- App-specific password or Notary API key configured in `notarytool` (for notarisation)
- `gh` CLI authenticated (`gh auth login`) for tagging and uploading assets

### Step-by-step

```
1. Bump the version (see checklist above)
2. Build → Archive in Xcode (Product → Archive)
3. Sign & notarise via Xcode Organizer:
     Distribute App → Direct Distribution → sign → notarise
     Export the notarised .app to disk
4. Wrap in a DMG:
     create-dmg Meridian.app --out Meridian-vX.Y.Z.dmg
     (or use hdiutil manually — any DMG with Meridian.app at the root works)
5. Staple the notarisation ticket to the DMG:
     xcrun stapler staple Meridian-vX.Y.Z.dmg
6. Tag and push the commit:
     git tag vX.Y.Z && git push origin vX.Y.Z
7. Create the GitHub release and attach the DMG:
     gh release create vX.Y.Z \
       --title "Meridian vX.Y.Z" \
       --notes "Release notes here" \
       Meridian-vX.Y.Z.dmg
```

### What happens automatically after publish

- Every running copy of Meridian checks GitHub Releases on next launch (rate-limited to once per 24 hours).
- Users can also trigger an immediate check via **Meridian → Check for Updates…** in the menu bar.
- `AppUpdateChecker` detects the new `vX.Y.Z` tag (canonical app tag = no suffix, all-numeric semver).
- If a `.dmg` asset is attached, the Settings → Updates tab shows a **"Download & Install vX.Y.Z"** button.
- Clicking it: downloads the DMG with a progress bar → mounts via `hdiutil` → copies `.app` over the running bundle → relaunches automatically. No user interaction beyond the button click.
- If no DMG is attached (rare), the button opens the GitHub release page in the browser instead.

### DMG asset naming

The asset filename must end in `.dmg`. The update checker matches the first asset with a `.dmg` suffix — the rest of the name does not matter. Convention:

```
Meridian-vX.Y.Z.dmg
```

### Engine release alongside app release

If the new app ships with a new engine:

```bash
# Publish engine first (app will auto-download it on first launch after update)
bash Scripts/release-engine.sh   # tags vX.Y.Z-engine and uploads to GitHub
```

Then proceed with the app release steps above. The engine update is detected and installed independently of the app update — users see both in Settings → Updates.

